A||||2||ezsurf||Temperature Guage
Z||000000||ezsurf||04-24-99||06:57 AM||||Last night was only the second time I have driven my Fiero.  I moved it to the shop where I am fixing miscellaneous problems.  I noticed last night that when I turned the ignition key to the on position, the temperature guage moved immediately to 182.5 degrees.  This became the "zero" point and it moved up from there. It peaked out at three tick marks past 220 degrees, I guess this would be 244 degrees(?)  From the 100 degree mark to the 220 degree mark, each tick mark represents 15 degrees.  From the 220 mark to the 260 degree mark, each tick mark represents 8 degrees (at least this is what the guage scale would indicate).  I'm sure I'm not the only one to have this problem.  Is this a problem with the guage, sending unit, or something else?
Z||000001||Bozone||04-27-99||06:04 PM||||In all likelyhood it's the needle getting set to fall off. Both my 86GTs have the needle sitting on the bottom of the lens case. There's a fix on the Michigan Fiero Club site I think because you have to take the pod off to fix it. I haven't fixed mine yet but no warm weather's here I have no excuse not to. Good luck.
Z||000002||theogre||04-27-99||07:13 PM||||pull the pod apart, or drop the coloumn and crawl under. neither is pretty.
